        <NEMO_annot:example rdf:datatype="&xsd;string">In a measurement process, the devices (=tools) used to detect, transform, represent, and record the data can be construed as &quot;instruments.&quot;</NEMO_annot:example>
        <NEMO_annot:comment rdf:datatype="&xsd;string">In linguistics, most arguments (NPs) of a relation can be classified in terms of three core participant (or &apos;thematic&apos;, &apos;theta&apos;) roles: &lt;AGENT&gt;, &lt;PATIENT&gt; (here termed &apos;object&apos;), and &lt;INSTRUMENT&gt;. Because these three argument roles are so central to the way humans conceptualize events, we are representing all three as subclasses of &lt;PARTICIPANT&gt;. We plan to have all three types of &lt;PARTICIPANT&gt; represented as subclasses of BFO:role if we maintain these relations. See also BioTop (bio-upper-ontology).</NEMO_annot:comment>
        <NEMO_annot:namespace rdf:datatype="&xsd;string">NEMO_relations</NEMO_annot:namespace>
        <NEMO_annot:comment rdf:datatype="&xsd;string">inspired by BioTop analog (is_means_of), though this relation is not defined in the owl ontology</NEMO_annot:comment>
        <NEMO_annot:pref_label rdf:datatype="&xsd;string">instrument_of</NEMO_annot:pref_label>
        <NEMO_annot:definition rdf:datatype="&xsd;string">instrument_of is a type of relation that takes a particular class of object (instruments --&gt; tools, resources) as its domain and a process as its range.</NEMO_annot:definition>
        <NEMO_annot:synonym rdf:datatype="&xsd;string">is_means_of</NEMO_annot:synonym>
        <NEMO_annot:curator rdf:resource="&ontology;NEMO_annotation_properties.owl#Gwen_Frishkoff"/>
        <NEMO_annot:curator rdf:resource="&ontology;NEMO_annotation_properties.owl#Snezana_Nikolic"/>
        <NEMO_annot:curation_status rdf:resource="&ontology;NEMO_annotation_properties.owl#definition_incomplete"/>
        <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="&ro;participates_in"/>
    </owl:ObjectProperty>
    


