        <NEMO_annot:definition rdf:datatype="&xsd;string">early-mid_post-event_latency is a type of event_related_latency_quality that characterizes the latency of an occurrent that is time-locked to an event as early-to-mid latency. &quot;Early-to-mid latency&quot; is operationally defined as 151-300 ms after the event boundary.</NEMO_annot:definition>
