        <NEMO_annot:definition rdf:datatype="&xsd;string">An postsynaptic potential (PSP) is a graded change in the membrane potential of a postsynaptic cell produced by a synaptic input, which alters the probability that the cell will fire an action potential.</NEMO_annot:definition>
