        <NEMO_annot:definition rdf:datatype="&xsd;string">A time constant is the time it takes the membrane potential to move 63% of the way toward its final value in response to the step change in current. Typical values are in the range of 1 to 20 ms.</NEMO_annot:definition>
        <NEMO_annot:definition_source rdf:datatype="&xsd;string">Kandel, E.R., Schwartz, J.H., &amp; Jessell, T.M. (Eds.). (1995). Essentials of neural science and behavior ( 1st Ed.), (pp. 708). Stamford, CT: Appleton &amp; Lange.</NEMO_annot:definition_source>
