        <NEMO_annot:modified_date rdf:datatype="&xsd;string">2010-08-01</NEMO_annot:modified_date>
        <NEMO_annot:definition rdf:datatype="&xsd;string">A unique code used by publishers in the identification and exchange of the content of a digital object, such as a journal article, web document, or other item of intellectual property. The DOI consists of two parts: a prefix assigned to each publisher by the administrative DOI agency and a suffix assigned by the publisher that may be any code the publisher chooses.</NEMO_annot:definition>
