        <NEMO_annot:definition rdf:datatype="&xsd;string">controlled_variable_role is the role of an experimental variable that is treated as a potential confound, e.g., because it is highly correlated with another variable of interest. To address this issue, the controlled variable is included in the statistical model. The goal is to show that the  variable of interest has a significant effect on the experiment outcome even when the variance due to the controlled measure is removed.</NEMO_annot:definition>
